Oh, from vlasisku I thought that the /preceding/ UI was what was dai'ed to the 
DOIed person.  E.g. "mi viska do .ue da'oi la .remo." for "I see you aren't you 
surprised la remo" vs "mi viska do .ue doi la .remo."  -> "I see you (surprised 
that it's /you/), remo"
